<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">August 27, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 181 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-08-27T07:12 UTC</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v48.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">&#9878; Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      MOU expiry without successor framework leaves Hormuz effectively closed at less than 4% of pre-war volume; Oman-Iran technical routing talks (<span class="cite">N2</span>, p=38%) remain the most immediate de-escalation path, while Mojtaba Khamenei's 172-day verified absence (<span class="cite">N4</span>, p=33%) constrains Iranian signatory authority for any replacement deal.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>&#9888; DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until &#8805;20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- 2. FORECAST BOARD -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">6 active · 7 resolved today · last reasoned 2026-08-27</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (&le;72h)</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N1</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will US forces conduct at least one confirmed airstrike on internationally recognized Iranian land territory before EOD 2026-08-30?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">12%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">new forecast (created 2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&#8594; resolves by 2026-08-30</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">CENTCOM conducted multiple rounds of strikes on Iranian territory throughout 2026. A 28-consecutive-night strike pause was in effect as of August 26-27. MOU expired August 17; Iran's "fully offensive" posture was declared the same day; active strike precedent is established but current pause period moderates near-term probability.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>CENTCOM press statement OR two independent TIER1 newswires (AP/Reuters/BBC) confirming a US kinetic airstrike on Iranian land territory within Iran's internationally recognized borders, after 2026-08-27T00:00Z.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM official statement preferred; minimum two independent TIER1 wire services required.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>IRGC naval vessel strikes inside Hormuz waters do not qualify. Offshore platform strikes resolve AMBIGUOUS unless CENTCOM specifies "Iranian territory." Cyber operations do not qualify. Disputed islands (Abu Musa, Tunbs): AMBIGUOUS pending Judge determination.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">USS Truman CSG AIS repositioning toward northern Arabian Sea</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump sub-72h ultimatum specifying Iran land targets</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM NOTAM activity over Iranian airspace</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N2</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran and Oman jointly announce a Strait of Hormuz commercial transit framework before EOD 2026-09-07?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">38%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">new forecast (created 2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&#8594; resolves by 2026-09-07</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran and Oman reached an "in principle" agreement on transit lane coordinates (inbound through Iranian waters, outbound through Omani waters) with a proposed 60-day trial and joint coordination center (i24News, mid-August). CNN and Al Jazeera (August 5) described parties as "close." Pakistan Army Chief Munir returned to Tehran August 24, keeping back-channel active. Residual obstacles: US political acquiescence and IRGC enforcement compliance.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>Official joint communique published simultaneously by both Oman's Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Iran's Foreign Ministry, OR US Secretary of State public confirmation of an Oman-brokered Hormuz transit agreement specifying bilateral Iranian agreement, before EOD 2026-09-07.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Oman FM official press release or TIER1 newswire with confirmed bilateral attribution.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Unilateral Omani or Iranian statements without counterpart confirmation do not qualify. Mediator language ("close," "progress") does not qualify. Must be a concrete, jointly attributed framework specifying transit conditions.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Omani FM Badr al-Busaidi confirmed travel to Tehran</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iranian Port and Maritime Organization softening statements on transit conditions</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US Secretary Rubio citing "deal reached" on Hormuz</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N3</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will ICE Brent crude front-month futures settle above $140.00/barrel on any single trading day before EOD 2026-09-10?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">13%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">new forecast (created 2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&#8594; resolves by 2026-09-10</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Current Brent settlement approximately $89-102 (CNBC August 19; Trading Economics August 26). Reaching $140 before September 10 requires a 38-57% move in 14 trading days — historically unprecedented. The Hormuz disruption is already priced into current levels. No identified incremental supply shock in the near-term indicator set would generate a $140 settlement. Judge reduced from initially proposed 0.31.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>ICE Brent front-month contract official settlement price exceeds $140.00/bbl on any trading session closing before EOD 2026-09-10, as recorded by Bloomberg, Reuters, or ICE Endex official settlement records.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Bloomberg, Reuters, or ICE Endex official settlement data.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Intraday spikes not holding at official settlement close do not qualify. WTI does not substitute for Brent. Options or forward contracts beyond front-month do not qualify.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Baltic Dirty Tanker Index week-on-week exceeding +15% on consecutive weeks</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Saudi spare capacity not deployed above 11.5 mb/d (removes downward price pressure)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM announcement of new large-scale Iran strike disrupting remaining Gulf export terminals</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-regime status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">regime</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Mojtaba Khamenei make a confirmed, independently verified public in-person appearance before EOD 2026-10-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">33%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">new forecast (created 2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&#8594; resolves by 2026-10-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">172 days have elapsed since Mojtaba Khamenei's last confirmed public appearance (March 8). Iranian state media disclosed in August that images would be released "soon" (globalsecurity.org/RFE/RL, August 9). J-Post reports an undated video of Khamenei teaching. Strict non-Iranian TIER1 standard constrains resolution paths; Assembly of Experts indicator is dormant (no September session scheduled). Oman/Qatar FM visit remains the most viable resolution mechanism.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>Video footage confirmed by two or more TIER1 international (non-Iranian) outlets showing Mojtaba Khamenei conducting official duties in person; OR an official foreign government diplomatic delegation publicly confirming an in-person meeting with Khamenei in an attributed statement accepted by at least one TIER1 outlet.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 outlets outside Iranian state media, or one TIER1 outlet plus an attributed foreign government official statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Written statements, audio, or still photographs without corroborating video or foreign diplomatic attestation do not qualify. Iranian state media alone does not satisfy the "independently verified" standard. Appearance at an event without a credible non-Iranian third-party witness does not qualify.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Assembly of Experts formal plenary session requiring Khamenei address</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Oman or Qatar FM confirmed travel to Tehran for bilateral meeting</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC senior commander citing direct orders from Khamenei in a named week</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Israel's October 27, 2026 general election be officially postponed to a date beyond November 10, 2026?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">7%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">new forecast (created 2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&#8594; resolves by 2026-10-28</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Knesset officially dispersed July 17 with election fixed for October 27. Postponement requires an 80-MK supermajority; current coalition bloc at 48-49 seats (Haaretz, August 26), far below 80. No Attorney General opinion on postponement permissibility has been issued. Bennett publicly stated "nobody will be allowed to postpone" the election. Structural supermajority constraint makes postponement extremely unlikely.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>Official announcement by the Israeli Central Elections Committee or Knesset standing committee order establishing a new election date later than November 10, 2026, published in Reshumot or reported by two TIER1 outlets with direct citation of official CEC announcement.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reshumot official publication or two TIER1 outlets citing official CEC announcement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Cabinet deliberations without a formal date change do not qualify. Postponement to any date on or before November 10 does not qualify. Postponement later reversed to October 27 resolves AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">AG extraordinary opinion supporting postponement permissibility</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Security Cabinet declaration of extraordinary security conditions</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Knesset Speaker written request to CEC for postponement review</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6–12 MONTHS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N6</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the IAEA formally report completion of Iran's down-blending of all &#8805;60%-enriched uranium stocks to &#8804;5% enrichment before EOD 2027-03-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">16%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">new forecast (created 2026-08-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&#8594; resolves by 2027-03-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">MOU (June 17) included a down-blending provision under IAEA monitoring, but the MOU expired August 17 without a successor framework. IAEA access status after August 17 is not publicly confirmed. Any resolution path requires: a new nuclear deal, restored IAEA continuous monitoring, physical down-blending operations, and IAEA full-completion certification — all within approximately 7 months. Long horizon preserves optionality; current trajectory is adverse.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>IAEA Director General report, Board of Governors formal document, or IAEA Secretariat press statement explicitly confirming full completion of Iran's down-blending of all near-bomb-grade (&#8805;60% LEU) stocks to &#8804;5% enrichment under IAEA continuous monitoring, published before EOD 2027-03-01.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IAEA.org official publication; TIER1 wire with direct attribution to IAEA DG statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Progress reports, partial-completion milestones, or IAEA access restoration without confirmed full completion do not qualify. If nuclear stocks are destroyed by military action and IAEA cannot verify compliance, resolve AMBIGUOUS pending Board assessment.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IAEA safeguards report documenting Fordow/Natanz configuration consistent with active down-blending</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">AEOI statement specifying enrichment reduction below 20% under IAEA supervision</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IAEA DG Grossi confirming "technical verification phase initiated" or "monitoring resumed"</span>
        </div>
      </div>

